### 🔍 Find Parent Node in BST (C Function)

```c
struct Node* findParent(struct Node* root, int key) {
    struct Node* parent = NULL;

    while (root != NULL && root->data != key) {
        parent = root;
        if (key < root->data)
            root = root->left;
        else
            root = root->right;
    }

    // If not found or key is root (no parent)
    if (root == NULL || parent == NULL)
        return NULL;

    return parent;
}
```

---

### 🛠 How to Use in `main()`

Add this test part in main:

```c
struct Node* p = findParent(root, 40);
if (p)
    printf("\nParent of 40 = %d", p->data);
else
    printf("\nNo Parent (maybe node is root or not present)");
```

---

### ⚡ What It Does
- Traverses the tree like search  
- Keeps track of previous node  
- Returns that previous node as parent  
- If node is root → returns NULL  
- If node not found → NULL  

